mmol) in 20 mL of CHCl3 was slowly added to a solution of 5 g (26 mmol)
of 2,4-dinitrofluorobenzene mixed with 7 mL of triethylamine at room
temperature. The purification was performed as described above for 1. A
yield of 5.2 g (79%). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 9.06 (s, 1H, -Ar, J m = 3.0 Hz);
δ 8.27 (dd, 1H, -Ar, J m = 3.0 Hz, J o = 9.0 Hz); δ 7.75 (d, 1H, -Ar, J o
= 9.0 Hz); δ 4.05 (t, 2H, -SCH2CH 2OH, J = 6.0 Hz); δ 3.30 (t, 2H, -SCH
2CH2OH, J = 6.0 Hz). Elemental analysis: (found) % C, 39.18; % H, 3.34; %
N, 11.37; % S, 13.12; (calculated) % C, 39.34; % H, 3.30; % N, 11.47; %
S, 13.13.
