$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of Aryl
Sulfides: To a stirred solution of iodobenzene (1.1 mmol) and
benzenethiol (1.0 mmol) in dry DMSO (2.0 mL) was added or (3.0 mol %)
followed by KOH (2.0 equiv) under nitrogen atmosphere at 135 °C for 24 h.
The progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC. After the reaction was
complete, the reaction mixture was allowed to cool, and a 1:1 mixture of
ethyl acetate/water (20 mL) was added The solvent and volatiles were
completely removed under vacuum to give the crude product, which was
purified by column chromatography (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate = 99:1)
to yield the expected product 1a (yield: In(OH)3 10% ; In2S3 15%).
decyl(p-tolyl)sulfane (2f) Following the general procedure using 4-methyl
iodobenzene and decanethiol provided decyl(p-tolyl)sulfane (208.70 mg)
with (79% yield). colorless oil IR (KBr): ν 3049, 2941, 2913, 1680, 1571,
1242, 1079, 974 cm-1. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ = 7.17 (d, 2H, J =
8.0 Hz), 7.01 (d, 2H, J = 8.0 Hz), 2.82 (t, 2H, J = 7.5 Hz), 2.31 (s,
3H), 1.59 (p, 2H, J = 7.5Hz), 1.42 - 1.17 (m, 14H), 0.88 (t, 3H, J = 7.0
Hz). 13C NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ = 135.7, 133.1, 129.7, 129.5, 34.3,
31.8, 29.5, 29.3, 29.2, 29.1, 28.8, 22.6, 20.9, 14.1. Mass (ESI): m/z 287
[M+Na]. Anal calcd for: (C17H28S) C: 77.20, H: 10.67, S: 12.12. found C:
77.12, H: 10.59, S: 11.99
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nano Indium Oxide as a Recyclable Catalyst for C-S Cross-Coupling of
