$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Experimental Procedure for the
Synthesis of Benzo[b]thiophene. In a 15 mL two-necked flask, a mixture of
(2-iodobenzyl)triphenylphosphonium bromide (168 mg, 0.3 mmol),
thiobenzoic acid (53 mg, 0.33 mmol), CuI (2.8 mg, 5% mol), and
1,10-phenthroline (5.2 mg, 10 mol %) in dioxane (3 mL) was stirred at
room temperature under N2 atmosphere for 5 min. Then the solution was
stirred at 100 &#x00B0;C for 32 h until complete consumption of starting
material as monitored by TLC. After the reaction was finished, the
mixture was washed with brine, extracted with EtOAc, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, and evaporated under a vacuum. The residue was purified by flash
column chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate, 8/1)
to give the product 3a. 6-Nitro-2-phenylbenzo[b]thiophene (3h). Brown
solid: 60.4 mg (79% yield). mp 196-197 &#x00B0;C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
&#x3B4; 8.79 (s, 1H), 8.25 (dd, J = 8.8, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 7.88 (d, J = 8.8
Hz, 1H), 7.77 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 7.66 (s, 1H), 7.49 (dt, J = 14.2, 6.9
Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) &#x3B4; 151.4, 145.1, 139.0, 133.2,
129.5, 129.2, 126.8, 123.6, 119.9, 119.0, 118.7. HRMS (EI) m/z [M+] calcd
for C14H9NO2S 255.0354, found 255.0362
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Ullmann coupling followed by Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-catalyzed synthesis of benzo[b]thiophenes and benzothiazoles using
thiocarboxylic acids as a coupling partner
