$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-tert-Butylsulfanyl-2’-nitrobiphenyl (31). To a stirred suspension of
Pd2(dba)3 (113 mg, 0.12 mmol) in EtOH (20 mL) was added
triphenylphosphine (129 mg, 0.49 mmol). After 10 min stirring, a solution
of 30 (2.0 g, 6.2 mmol) in EtOH (40 mL) was added, followed by the
addition of benzenethiol (763 μL, 6.8 mmol) and potassium tert-butoxide
(1.38 g, 12.3 mmol). The resulting solution was heated to reflux for 8 h,
then cooled to room temperature, filtered through a pad of Celite and
washed with CH2Cl2 (100 mL). The solvent was removed, and the residue was
dissolved in CH2Cl2 (100 mL) then washed with water (2 x 50 mL) and satd.
aq. NaCl (50 mL). The aqueous layer was then extracted with EtOAc (100
mL) and the combined organic extracts were dried and concentrated to
yield the crude product. Purification by flash column chromatography over
silica gel (eluting with 50% CH2Cl2 in hexanes) gave 31 (1.39 g, 79%) as
a brown solid. M.p. 68-70 °C; 1H NMR (500 MHz) δ: 8.07 (dd, J = 1.0, 8.0
Hz, 1H), 7.66 (dd, J = 1.0, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.62 (dt, J = 1.0, 7.5 Hz, 1H),
7.51 (dt, J = 1.5, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.44 (dt, J = 1.5, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.39 -
7.32 (m, 3H), 1.08 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (125 MHz) δ: 149.3, 144.3, 138.3,
137.0, 133.6, 132.2, 131.8, 129.6, 128.9, 128.2, 128.0, 124.1, 47.5,
31.1; EIHRMS Calcd. for C16H17NO2S: 287.0980. Found: 287.1005 [M+ .].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Is There a Homolytic Substitution Chemistry (SH2) of Sulfones?
