$DATUM 5,10,15-tri(4-pyridyl)-20-(4-(1',5'-dithiopentyl)-2,3,5,6-tetrafluorophenyl)porphyrin(TPy3PF4-SC5SH
; 2) .A mixture of 1 (15 mg, 21.2 μmol), 1,5-pentanedithiol (25 μL, 180.5
μmol and diethyl amine (60 μL, 580 μmol) were stirred in a solvent
mixture of DMF, chloroform and methanol (4:4:1 v/v, 3 mL) in the dark
under nitrogen at room temperature for 24h. After evaporation of the
solvent at reduced pressure, the crude product was purified by flash
column chromatography on silica gel with dichloromethane/methanol, 97%
CH2Cl2 / 3% CH3OH (v/v). Yield (13.8mg, 79%). UV- visible in CH2Cl2 :
λmax nm (rel. intensity): 416 (100), 511 (9.28), 544 (3.85), 585 (4.25)
and 640 (2.39). 1H NMR (500MHz, CDCl3):δ = 9.10 (d, J = 5.3 Hz, 6H), 8.91
(m, 8H), 8.20 (m, 6H), 3.31 (t, 2H), 2.67 (m, 2H), 1.91 (m, 2H), 1.79 (m,
4H), 1.45 (t, 1H) and -2.81 (s, 2H). ESI-MS : 824 (MH+)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Characterization of a Thiol-Tethered Tripyridyl Porphyrin
on Au(111)
