$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1,4-Bis[isopropylthio]benzene(3); Typical
Procedure for Runs 1-6 (Table 1): A solution of 1,4-clichlorobenzene
(1.47 g, 10 mmol) and sodium 2- propanethiolate (4.9 g, 50 mmol) in
dimethylformamide (30 ml) is stirred under nitrogen for 17 h at 100°C,
The progress of the reaction is monitored by T.L.C. and G.L.C. The
mixture is cooled, poured into water (100 ml) and extracted with ether (3
× 50 mI). The organic layer is washed with water (2 × 50 ml), dried with
sodium sulphate, and evaporated. The residue (a single spot on T.L.C.) is
chromatographed through a silica gel column using light petroleum as
eluent. run 5, Equiv. of reagent 3, temperature 100°C, time 17 h, Yield
79%.
