$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-(tert-Butylthio)-N-(2,6-dimethylphenyl)-5-nitrobenzamide (5a). Amide
(4a) (6.43 mmol; 1.96 g) was added to the solution of tert-butylthiol
(7.72 mmol; 0.70 g; 0.5 ml) and sodium hydroxide (7,07 mmol; 0.28 g) in
DMF (10 ml) at 0°C. It was stirred at 0°C for 3h. After that
tert-butylthiol (20 mol%) was added and it was stirred for another 0.5h.
The mixture was poured in to the ice cold 5% hydrochloric acid, the
precipitated solid was filtered and washed with water. After drying pure
tert-butythiolether was obtained as a yellowish crystalline solid in 96%
yield (2.20 g). 2-(tert-Butylthio)-N-(2-hydroxyethyl)-5-nitrobenzamide
(5b). The general procedure was used employing amide (4b) (3.2 g; 13.08
mmol) and the reaction was complete after 3h. The product was obtained as
a yellowish solid in 79% yield (3.11 g). M.p. 103.5-105°C
(toluene/hexane). 1H NMR (400 MHz, Acetone): δ 8.41 (d, J= 2.6, 1H), 8.25
(dd, J= 2.7, 8.5, 1H), 8.01 (br s, 1H), 7.91 (d, J= 8.5, 1H), 3.92 (t, J=
5.5, 1H), 3.78- 3.72 (m, 2H), 3.54 (q, J= 5.7, 2H), 1.36 (s, 9H). 13C NMR
(101 MHz, Acetone): δ 167.6, 148.8, 145.3, 140.5, 140.0, 124.8, 124.6,
62.0, 49.9, 44.0, 32.0. IR (CHCl3): 3627 w (OH), 3437 w (NH), 3287 w
(NH), 2966 w (CH3), 1658 s (CONH), 1526 s (NO2), 1472 w (CH3), 1367 m
(CH3), 1350 s (NO2), 1067 w (OH) cm-1 . Anal. calcd for C13H18N2O4S: C,
52.33; H, 6.08; N, 9.39. Found: C, 52.12; H, 6.07; N, 9.27.
