$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General experimental procedure A 25 mL Wattecs
reaction tube was charged with 2-haloaniline 1 (0.6 mmol), potassium
O-ethyl dithiocarbonate 2 (1.8 mmol), CuCl (0.06 mmol), and DMF (2 mL).
The reaction vessel was flushed with argon three times and sealed. Then
the mixture was stirred electromagnetically in an oil bath at 110°C for 6
h. The reaction process was monitored by TLC on silica gel. After the
reaction was completed, the reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, and then HCl (3 mL, 3 mol/L) was added and stirred for
another 30 min. The reaction mixture solution was extracted by ethyl
acetate (3 × 20 mL). Subsequently, the combined organic solutions were
dried by anhydrous sodium sulfate and the target product was purified by
chromatography on a silica gel column (eluent: petroleum ether/ethyl
acetate) to give the corresponding pure product 3.
2-mercaptobenzothiazole (3a) 1 6-bromo-2-mercaptobenzothiazole (3d)1 3d
was obtained as a yellow solid. M.p. 264-267 ºC; 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO,
TMS): δ 13.86 (brs, 1H), 7.98 (d, 1H, J = 2.0 Hz), 7.56 (dd, 1H, J 1 =
8.5 Hz, J 2 = 2.0 Hz), 7.22 (d, 1H, J = 8.5 Hz); 13C NMR (125 MHz, DMSO,
TMS): δ 190.1, 140.5, 131.4, 129.9, 124.1, 116.3, 113.8; MS (EI+): m/z
calcd for C7H5BrNS2 [M+H]+: 247.90, found 247.0; Anal. Calcd. for
C7H4BrNS2: C, 34.16; H, 1.64; N, 5.69; Found: C, 34.45; H, 1.38; N, 5.51.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM reaction in a sealed vessel, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An efficient copper-catalyzed synthesis of 2-mercaptobenzothiazoles
through S-arylation/heterocyclization of 2-haloanilines with potassium
xanthate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liu, Lei; Zhu, Ning; Gao, Min; Zhao, Xiaole; Han, Limin; Hong, Hailong
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Phosphorus, Sulfur and Silicon and the Related Elements (2016), 191(5),
699-701

