$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Diphenyl Thioether (2a); Typical Procedure. A
flame-dried test tube with a magnetic stirring bar was charged with CuBr
(14 mg, 0.1 mmol), ligand (15 mg, 0.1 mmol), Cs2CO3 (326 mg, 1.0 mmol),
thiophenol (55 mg, 0.5 mmol), bromobenzene (118 mg, 0.75 mmol), and DMF
(1.5 mL) under argon. The mixture was stirred at 130 °C for 48 h, then
cooled to r.t. and the resulting mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 25
mL). The combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated
under vacuum. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica
gel with PE as eluent. This compound was prepared as shown in Scheme 2
employing the molar ratios of the starting materials used for the
preparation of 3a. The crude product was purified over a silica gel
column using PE. 4-Bromophenyl Phenyl Thioether as colorless oil (CAS:
65662-88-6), yield 78%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.39 (d, J = 8.4 Hz,
2 H), 7.36-7.24 (m, 5 H), 7.16 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 135.7, 135.0, 132.4, 132.2, 131.7, 129.5, 127.7, 121.0. GC-MS
(EI): m/z = 264 [M]+, 266 [M + 2]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM product depends on stoichiometry,temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient copper-catalyzed S-arylation of thiols with aryl bromides and
chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Yaming; Li, Xiaoying; Wang, Huifeng; Chen, Tao; Xie, Yusheng
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2010), (21), 3602-3608

