$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,5-Di(phenylthio)phthalimide. This compound was formed from by adding
triethylamine (0.47 g, 4.6 mmol) dropwise to a mixture of
4,5-dibromophthalimide (0.61 g, 2.0 mmol) and thiophenol (0.51 g, 4.6
mmol) in 5 mL of N,N-dimethylformamide. The stirred reaction mixture was
kept at room temperature for 1 h and then at 50-55 °C for 40 min. After
the mixture was cooled and poured into water, the precipitate was
filtered off, washed with water, and crystallized from acetic acid.
Yellow crystals were obtained (yield: 0.50 g, 78%). Anal. (Calcd, Found
for C20H13NO2S2): C (66.09, 65.78), H (3.60, 3.45), N (3.85, 3.82),
S(17.64, 17.61). Mp: 258-260 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
