$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of OCMe2CMe2OP(S)SC6H4NO2 p-bromonitrobenzene (0.96 gm) was
dissolved in 30 ml benzene. To this, a solution of ammonium
tetramethylene dithiophosphate (1.09 gm) was added slowly and refluxed
for ~10 h. The precipitated ammonium bromide was filtered off. The
solvent was removed from the filtrate under reduced pressure to obtain
the desired product, yellow sticky solid. The above procedure was adopted
for all the other reactions. Relevant data are given in Table II.
OCMe2CMe2OP(S)SC6H4NO2, yield 1.24 g, 78%. 1H (δ ppm) 1.6, S, 12H (CH3);
7.5, m, 4H (C6H4), 31p (δ ppm) 94.09. The compound on analyses show: C,
42.98; H, 4.58; N, 18.83%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic derivatives of alkylene dithiophosphates part III: Synthesis and
properties of 2-(p-nitrophenyl) and 2-(p-nitrobenzoyl) derivatives of
alkylene dithiophosphates
