$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure B: To a 10 mL glass tube,
CuBr (2.8 mg, 0.02 mmol), 1,10-phenanthroline (3.6 mg, 0.02 mmol), AgSCF3
(62.7 mg, 0.3 mmol), and arylhalide (0.2 mmol) were dissolved in dry DMF
(1 mL) under N2 atmosphere. The tube was sealed and the mixture was
stirred at the corresponding temperature for 6 h. After completion of the
reaction, the mixture was directly subjected to flash column
chromatography on silica gel with a gradient eluent of petroleum ether
and ethyl acetate (range from 20:1 to 5:1). The product.
(S)-5-(tert-butyl)-2-(2-((trifluoromethyl)thio)phenyl)-4,5-dihydrooxazole
(4i) This reaction was conducted with procedure B in 0.2 mmol scale. The
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel with a
gradient eluent of petroleum ether and ethyl acetate (5:1 - 3:1). The
product 4i (52 mg, 78% yield) as yellow oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.80 (dd, J = 7.2, 1.2 Hz 1H), 7.72 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.45 (td, J =
8.0, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.39 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 4.35 (dd, J = 9.6, 8.8 Hz,
1H), 4.24 (t, J = 8.0 Hz 1H), 4.13 (dd, J = 10.0, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 0.99 (s,
9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 161.8, 132.0 (q, J = 1.5 Hz), 131.0,
130.3, 130.0, 129.6 (q, J = 308 Hz), 128.3, 127.9 (q, J = 1.5 Hz), 77.1,
68.9, 40.0, 25.8. 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3) δ -41.63 (s). HRMS: m/z (ESI)
calculated [M+H]+: 304.0977, measured: 304.0977.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-Catalyzed Trifluoromethylthiolation of Aryl Halides with Diverse
Directing Groups
