$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Synthesis of
2-Fluorophenyl 2-Nitrophenyl Ether 7a and Thioether 7b: 2-Fluorophenol or
2-fluorothiophenol (20 mmol) was added dropwise under nitrogen to a
solution of 1-chloro-2-nitrobenzene (4.73 g, 30 mmol) and solid copper
oxide (I) (4.29 g, 30 mmol) in pyridine (50 mL) at room temperature. The
resulting mixture was heated at reflux for 12 h, cooled to room
temperature, and treated with HCl (1 M). The mixture was extracted with
Et2O (3 x 50 mL), and the combined organic layers were washed with
saturated Na2CO3 aqueous solution and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The
solvents were removed under reduced pressure and the residue was purified
by silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc) to provide the
corresponding ether or thioether: 2-Fluorophenyl 2-nitrophenyl thioether
(7b): Prepared from 2-fluorothiophenol (2.56 g, 20 mmol), Cu2O (4.29 g,
30 mmol) and 1-chloro-2-nitrobenzene (4.73 g, 30 mmol) in pyridine (50
mL) according to the above procedure to give the title compound (3.89 g,
78%) as a yellow solid: mp 80-82 °C (lit.4 mp 75 °C); 1H NMR (200 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 8.23 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.66-7.14 (m, 6H), 6.82 (dd, J = 7.8,
1.3 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (50.3 MHz, CDCl3) δ 163.0 (d, J = 251.3 Hz, C),
144.9 (C), 137.7 (CH), 137.3 (C), 133.6 (CH), 132.8 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, CH),
127.5 (CH), 125.8 (CH), 125.5 (d, J = 3.8 Hz, CH), 125.2 (CH), 117.9 (d,
J = 19.4 Hz, C), 116.7 (d, J = 22.9 Hz, CH); EI-LRMS m/z 249 (M+, 33),
185 (100); HRMS calcd for C12H8FNO2S, 249.0260; found, 249.0269.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Route to Regioselectively Functionalized Carbazoles, Dibenzofurans, and
Dibenzothiophenes through Anionic Cyclization of Benzyne-Tethered
Aryllithiums
