$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4,5-Bis(hexylthio)phthalonitrile (1a). A
mixture of hexane-1-thiol (6.0 g, 50.7 mmol), K2CO3 (14.0 g, 101.3 mmol),
and DMSO (200 mL) was stirred at ambient temperature for 30 min.
Dichlorophthalonitrile (4.0 g, 20.3 mmol) was added, and the reaction
mixture was maintained at 80 °C for 12 h. The reaction mixture was
allowed to cool to ambient temperature, quenched with brine (100 mL),
extracted into ether (2 x 100 mL), and washed with water (2 x 100 mL),
and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure to obtain a yellow
solid. Activated carbon was used to decolorize the compound, when
necessary. Further purification using flash chromatography (SiO2, 10:90
ethyl acetate/hexanes). 4,5-Bis(nonylthio)phthalonitrile (1d) as a
colorless solid, yield 2.6 g, 78%. mp 74-76 °C; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.38 (s, 2H), 3.00-2.98 (t, J = 10 Hz, 4H), 1.74-1.71 (p, J = 15 Hz, 4H),
1.48-1.45 (p, J = 15 Hz, 4H), 1.34-1.27 (m, 20H), 0.88-0.86 (t, J = 10
Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 144.2, 128.1, 115.6, 111.0, 32.8,
31.9, 29.4, 29.2, 29.1, 28.9, 28.1, 22.7, 14.1; MS (EI) m/z 444.2 [M]+,
C26H40N2S2 requires 444.2. Anal. Calcd for C26H40N2S2: C, 70.22; H, 9.07;
N, 6.30. Found: C, 69.92; H, 9.12; N, 6.39.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM third stage quench
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solvent-Free Synthesis of Soluble, Near-IR Absorbing Titanyl
Phthalocyanine Derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mayukh, Mayank; Sema, Clarissa M.; Roberts, Jessica M.; McGrath, Dominic
V.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(22), 7893-7896

