$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-[2-(4-Bromophenylthio)phenyl]acetic Acid (2). A sealed tube containing
2-iodophenylacetic acid (1g, 3.82 mmol), 4-bromobenzenethiol (721.7 mg,
3.82 mmol), potassium hydroxide (427.8 mg, 7.64 mmol), copper powder
(24.27 mg, 0.382 mmol), and water (1.9 mL) was submitted to microwave
irradiation (two cycles of 6 min each at power 180 W, Tmax = 140 °C, 100
psi); the sample was cooled during irradiation with a flow of compressed
air. The obtained suspension was dissolved in a solution of 2 N KOH and
then fitered. The filtrate was acidified with 1 N HCl, and the formed
precipitate was fitered and dried under reduced pressure (T = 50 °C).
(960 mg, 2.97 mmol, 77% yield). white precipitate. 1H-NMR (DMSO-d6) δ:
3.74 (s, 2H), 7.07 (d, J =8.42 Hz, 2H), 7.30-7.39 (m, 1H), 7.36-7.43 (m,
3H), 7.48 (d, J =8.42 Hz, 2H). 13C-NMR (DMSO-d6) δ: 120.03, 128.98,
129.54, 131.08, 132.34, 132.71, 133.25, 134.97, 136.64, 138.62, 172.57.
MS for C14H1179BrO2S: m/z calculated 323.2, found 346.02. [M + Na]+,
668.94 [2M + Na]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (180 W), Ullmann-type reaction, sealed tube used
