$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method C: 2-Arylthio-6-fluorothiobenzonitrile
(10). The procedure is similar to that reported in ref 23. Thus, to an
ice-bath-cooled suspension of potassium t-butoxide or potassium carbonate
in dry DMSO or DMF was added 1-1.1 molar equiv of arylthiol 7, followed
by a molar equivalent of 2,6-difluorobenzonitrile (9). The resultant
mixture was stirred for 1 h and was then poured into H2O. This was
followed by stirring for about 30 min. Intermediate 10 was collected by
filtration and dried. This intermediate was either used without
purification or subjected to flash column chromatography on silica gel
using solvents. 10z, yield 77%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solvent and base assumed
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
