$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Decakis(1-dodecylthio)corannulene (10). Decachlorocorannulene7 (7, 20 mg,
0.03 mmol) and sodium 1-dodecanethiolate (66 mg, 0.67 mmol), prepared as
above from 1-dodecanethiol and sodium in absolute EtOH, were stirred in
3.0 mL of 1,3-dimethylimidazolidin- 2-one (DMEU) at r.t. under nitrogen
for 5 d. During the reaction period, the mixture changed color from
reddish brown to deep green. The reaction mixture was then added to
toluene (30 mL) and washed with H2O (5 X 30 mL) and sat. NaCl solution (3
X 30 mL). The organic layer was dried with anhyd MgSO4 and concentrated
to dryness under reduced pressure to give a red oil. Chromatography on
silica gel (petroleum ether/Et2O = 95/5) gave dodecyldisulfide as a
by-product (faster moving on silica gel) and the
decakis(1-dodecylthio)corannulene (10). Orange oil, yield 58 mg, 77%. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 3.03 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 20 H), 1.57 (m, 20 H),
1.34 (m, 20 H), 1.18 (m, 160 H), 0.85 (t, J= 6.8 Hz, 30 H). 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 141.82, 133.86, 131.95, 40.23, 32.15, 29.93, 29.89,
29.83, 29.70, 29.61, 29.58, 29.33, 22.91, 14.34. UV/VIS (CH3CN): λmax =
390, 313, 265 nm. HRMS: calcd for C140H250S10(M+): 2251.6770. Found:
2251.6755.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM other product also detected, thiol salt prepared independently in solid
form
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Corannulene polysulfides: Molecular bowls with multiple arms and flaps
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bancu, Mihail; Rai, Amarjit K.; Cheng, Peichao; Gilardi, Richard D.;
Scott, Lawrence T.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2004), (1), 173-176

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME406 STEP1
