$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
precursor 50-57. A mixture of the corresponding thiol (1 eq), KOH (1 eq)
and methanol (~3 mL per 1 mmol thiol) was stirred at room temperature
until the KOH was dissolved. After evaporation of the solvent under
reduced pressure, the thiolate was dissolved in anhydrous DMF (~3 mL per
1 mmol thiol). The corresponding para-haloginated-benzaldehyde (1eq) was
added to the stirred mixture in small portions at 0°C. The reaction
mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature and was stirred till TLC
indicated completion. The reaction mixture was partitioned between ether
20 mL and 10 mL H2O. The aqueous layer was washed with ether (3 x 25 mL)
and the combined organic layers were washed with 10 mL of H2O and 10 mL
brine, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was
purified by silica gel column chromatography using n-hexane/EtOAc
mixtures or by recrystallization from isopropyl alcohol to give the pure
product. Reaction batch: Cyclohexanethiol 65 (630 mg, 5.4 mmol);
4-chlor-3-nitrobenzaldehyde (1.0 g, 5.4 mmol). Reaction batch:
4-(Trifluoromethoxy)benzenethiol 71 (311 mg, 1.6 mmol),
4-chlor-3-nitrobenzaldehyde (297 mg, 1.6 mmol).
3-Nitro-4-((4-(trifluoromethoxy)phenyl)thio)benzaldehyde as a yellow
solid, yield 430 mg, 1.3 mmol, 77%. M.p.: 96°C; TLC: (PE : EtOAc, 5:1):
Rf = 0.56. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.99 (s, 1H), 8.71 (d, J = 1.7 Hz,
1H), 7.85 (dd, J = 8.5, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.71 - 7.59 (m, 2H), 7.38 (d, J =
8.5 Hz, 2H), 6.99 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ
189.04, 151.21, 151.20, 146.50, 144.98, 137.81, 133.53, 132.27, 128.74,
128.29, 127.88, 122.70, 120.47 (q, J = 259.0 Hz). 19F-NMR (376 MHz,
CDCl3): δ [ppm] = -57.69. CHN analysis: calculated: C, 48.98; H, 2.35; N,
4.08; found: C, 48.56; H, 2.72; N, 4.18.
